CustomerDashboardForm.cs and AdminDashboardForm.cs:

It would be best to review tutorials or documentations to learn how to display and manage product catalogs in Windows Forms. You will need to create or fetch appliance objects and bind them to DataGridView or ListView controls, adding functionalities for searching, calculating total price, and adding orders. Here are some resources to start with:

- DataGridView documentation: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/desktop/winforms/controls/datagridview-control-overview?view=netframeworkdesktop-4.8
- ListView documentation: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/desktop/winforms/controls/using-the-listview-control?view=netframeworkdesktop-4.8
- Tutorial on displaying data with DataGridView: https://www.c-sharpcorner.com/UploadFile/mahesh/DataGridViewTutorialCSharpWinForms11122005071203AM/DataGridViewTutorialCSharpWinForms.aspx
- Related SO post for product catalogs: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/22170809/how-to-create-a-basic-product-catalog-in-net-windows-application

Overall, great job so far! Continue refining the code for the assigned tasks, and you will have a complete home appliance rental application.

